with

```clojure
(let [city (if (= @lang :uk) (get-in conf [:city :uk]) (get-in conf [:city :en]))
      title (if (= @lang :uk) (get-in conf [:title :uk]) (get-in conf [:title :en]))
      text (if (= @lang :uk) (get-in conf [:text :uk]) (get-in conf [:text :en]))]
```

Then use `city`, `title`, `text` directly in the markup. Cleaner, no runtime fn spam.

